# visible surface matches `pnpm <path> --help` on the root and all
# 112 command paths (`test`, `start` and `stop` forward --help to
# the package script).
#
# Items marked "(hidden)" are accepted by pnpm but never shown by --help;
# each one was confirmed against the binary with `pnpm <path> <item> --help`
# (prints help) next to a `--zz-definitely-not-a-flag` control (rejected):
#
#   * (`rb` is a clap command of its own, not an alias of `rebuild`)
#   * every boolean flag has a hidden `--no-<flag>` negation added at parse
#     time (215 of them across all scopes);
#   * <root>: --prefix (alias for --dir), --store (alias for --store-dir),
#              --no-color, --progress, --reporter-hide-prefix,
#              --no-reporter-hide-prefix, --no-reverse, --resume-from,
#              --no-bail, --bail, --report-summary, --if-present
#   * add: --no-ignore-workspace-root-check
#   * ci: --verify-deps-before-run-install
#   * deploy: --verify-deps-before-run-install
#   * env: --remote
#   * install: --verify-deps-before-run-install
#   * install-test: --verify-deps-before-run-install
#   * pack: --no-skip-manifest-obfuscation
#   * pipeline: --verify-deps-before-run-install
#   * publish: --no-embed-readme, --no-skip-manifest-obfuscation
#   * rb: --no-pending
#   * rebuild: --no-pending
#   * stage: --no-embed-readme, --no-skip-manifest-obfuscation
#   * tasks: <args> positional
#   * 39 config settings accepted as bare flags on every command
#     (`--<setting>`, plus `--no-<setting>` for the boolean ones):
#       allow-unused-patches child-concurrency dangerously-allow-all-builds
#       engine-strict force-legacy-deploy frozen-store global-dir hoist
#       hoist-pattern ignore-pnpmfile ignore-scripts link-workspace-packages
#       lockfile lockfile-include-tarball-url merge-git-branch-lockfiles
#       modules-dir node-experimental-package-map offline
#       optimistic-repeat-install package-import-method pm-on-fail
#       prefer-frozen-lockfile prefer-offline public-hoist-pattern
#       runtime-on-fail save-workspace-protocol shamefully-hoist
#       shared-workspace-lockfile side-effects-cache
#       side-effects-cache-readonly strict-peer-dependencies trust-lockfile
#       trust-policy trust-policy-exclude trust-policy-ignore-after
#       unsafe-perm verify-store-integrity virtual-store-dir
#       virtual-store-only
#   * `--config.<key>=<value>` for any config key, and `-s`/`--silent`
#     (rewritten to --reporter=silent; `run -s` keeps its own --sequential);
#   * the `pm` prefix (`pnpm pm <cmd>` forces the built-in command over a
#     same-named script);
#   * `pnpm install <pkg>`, which pnpm rewrites to `pnpm add <pkg>`;
#   * hand-dispatched words that a command's own help or error message lists
#     under one spelling only: env ls/rm/uninstall/un, shim remove/uninstall/
#     list, team list. Commands whose help says only "Subcommand and
#     arguments" (access, dist-tag, licenses, owner, stage, ...) have no
#     documented word list, so their words are completed unmarked.
#
# Also completed: `recursive`/`multi`/`m` and `with <version|current>` as
# prefixes of another pnpm command line, `pnpm <script>` (the script
# fallback), and the `pnpx`/`pnx` wrappers (`pnpm dlx`).
#
# Left out on purpose:
#   * `completion-server`: the hidden endpoint shell scripts call. It is
#     used here as the value source for scripts and workspace packages.
#   * `completion <shell>`'s hidden trailing arguments (always an error).
#   * `--<flag>=true|false` spellings of boolean flags (accepted, rewritten
#     to the flag or its negation before parsing).
#   * abbreviations: pnpm does not infer them (`pnpm instal` runs a script).
#
